            Attribute flags that transform the final value (--LL, --RR, --ZZ, --ll,
            --uu) are only applied to the expanded value at the point of a
            parameter expansion expression using `$$'.  They are not applied
            when a parameter is retrieved internally by the shell for any
            purpose.

            The following attribute flags may be specified:

            --AA     The names refer to associative array parameters; see `Array
                   Parameters' in _z_s_h_p_a_r_a_m(1).

            --LL [ _n ]
