            Wait for the specified jobs or processes.  If _j_o_b is not given
            then all currently active child processes are waited for.  Each
            _j_o_b can be either a job specification or the process ID of a job
            in the job table.  The exit status from this command is that of
            the job waited for.  If _j_o_b represents an unknown job or process
            ID, a warning is printed (unless the PPOOSSIIXX__BBUUIILLTTIINNSS option is set)
            and the exit status is 127.

